        <div id="sqty">
            <div class="BackgroundWhite PaddingYTwentyFour SmallBreakpointPaddingYThirtyTwo">
                <div class="MarginXAuto MaxWidthSevenXL PaddingXSix LargeBreakpointPaddingXEight">
                    <div class="MarginXAuto MaxWidthTwoXL LargeBreakpointTextCenter">
                        <p class="MarginTopTwo TextSizeThreeXL BoldFont TightTracking TextGrayNineHundred SmallBreakpointTextSizeFourXL">A Considered Approach to Interior Design</p>
                        <p class="MarginTopSix LargeTextSize LeadingEight TextGraySixHundred">
                            A successful interior is more than a collection of attractive objects: it should make sense for the people who use it and the way the space is arranged. Roomcraft Interiors brings together practical planning and visual decisions, so layout, colour, materials, lighting and furniture can be considered as parts of one coherent direction. The starting point is your brief, preferences and questions, not a predetermined style.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="MarginXAuto MarginTopSixteen MaxWidthTwoXL SmallBreakpointMarginTopTwenty LargeBreakpointMarginTopTwentyFour LargeBreakpointMaxWidthFourXL">
                        <dl class="GridContainer MaxWidthXL GridColumnsOne GapXEight GapYTen LargeBreakpointMaxWidthNone LargeBreakpointGridColumnsTwo LargeBreakpointGapYSixteen">
                            <div class="RelativePosition PaddingLeftSixteen">
                                <dt class="BaseTextSize SemiboldFont LeadingSeven TextGrayNineHundred">
                                    <div class="AbsolutePosition LeftZero TopZero FlexContainer HeightTen WidthTen ItemsCenterAlign JustifyContentCenter LargeRoundedCorners BackgroundSkySixHundred WhiteText">
                                        <svg class="WidthSix HeightSix" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" id="u0eci" data-name="Layer 1" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="512" height="512">
                                            <path
                                                d="M23,17a1,1,0,0,0-1,1v2.586l-2.994-2.994C21.2,15.25,23,12.547,23,9.987a5.745,5.745,0,0,0-5.5-5.949A5.39,5.39,0,0,0,13,6.57,5.39,5.39,0,0,0,8.5,4.038a5.13,5.13,0,0,0-2.428.619L1.707.293A1,1,0,0,0,.293,1.707L4.5,5.915A6.188,6.188,0,0,0,3,9.987c0,3.791,3.951,7.9,7.265,10.676a4.248,4.248,0,0,0,5.47,0c.608-.51,1.238-1.065,1.861-1.654L20.586,22H18a1,1,0,0,0,0,2h4a2,2,0,0,0,2-2V18A1,1,0,0,0,23,17Zm-8.55,2.132a2.311,2.311,0,0,1-2.9,0C7.387,15.643,5,12.31,5,9.987A3.749,3.749,0,0,1,8.5,6.038,3.749,3.749,0,0,1,12,9.987a1,1,0,1,0,2,0,3.749,3.749,0,0,1,3.5-3.949A3.749,3.749,0,0,1,21,9.987C21,12.309,18.612,15.642,14.45,19.132Z"
                                            ></path>
                                        </svg>
                                    </div>
                                    Begin With How You Use the Space
                                </dt>
                                <dd class="MarginTopTwo BaseTextSize LeadingSeven TextGraySixHundred">
                                    Before considering finishes or furnishings, it helps to understand what a room needs to do. Think about who uses it, when it is busiest, what activities take place there and which items need a home. These everyday details can guide decisions about circulation, furniture placement, storage and lighting. A clear brief gives the design conversation a practical foundation, while leaving room for your taste and ideas to shape the atmosphere.
                                </dd>
                            </div>
                            <div class="RelativePosition PaddingLeftSixteen">
                                <dt class="BaseTextSize SemiboldFont LeadingSeven TextGrayNineHundred">
                                    <div class="AbsolutePosition LeftZero TopZero FlexContainer HeightTen WidthTen ItemsCenterAlign JustifyContentCenter LargeRoundedCorners BackgroundSkySixHundred WhiteText">
                                        <svg class="WidthSix HeightSix" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" id="u0eci" data-name="Layer 1" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                                            <path
                                                d="m22,5.735v-3.735c0-.553-.447-1-1-1s-1,.447-1,1v2.367L14.797.855c-1.699-1.146-3.895-1.146-5.594,0L2.204,5.579c-1.38.931-2.204,2.479-2.204,4.145v9.276c0,2.757,2.243,5,5,5h14c2.757,0,5-2.243,5-5v-9.276c0-1.579-.748-3.047-2-3.989Zm0,13.265c0,1.654-1.346,3-3,3H5c-1.654,0-3-1.346-3-3v-9.276c0-.999.494-1.928,1.322-2.486l7-4.724c.51-.345,1.094-.517,1.678-.517s1.168.172,1.678.517l7.001,4.724c.827.558,1.321,1.487,1.321,2.486v9.276Zm-7.788-10.077c-.906,0-1.684.284-2.25.775-.567-.491-1.344-.775-2.25-.775-1.792,0-3.25,1.56-3.25,3.476,0,2.205,2.271,4.491,4.177,6.021.383.308.853.461,1.323.461s.94-.153,1.324-.462c1.905-1.529,4.177-3.815,4.177-6.021,0-1.916-1.458-3.476-3.25-3.476Zm-2.178,7.937c-.041.033-.103.032-.144,0-2.115-1.698-3.428-3.408-3.428-4.462,0-.813.561-1.476,1.25-1.476.57,0,1.25.187,1.25,1.077,0,.553.448,1,1,1s1-.447,1-1c0-.891.68-1.077,1.25-1.077.689,0,1.25.662,1.25,1.476,0,1.054-1.313,2.764-3.428,4.461Z"
                                            ></path>
                                        </svg>
                                    </div>
                                    Bring Visual Choices Together
                                </dt>
                                <dd class="MarginTopTwo BaseTextSize LeadingSeven TextGraySixHundred">
                                    Colours, textures and materials can feel very different when considered separately from the room they will inhabit. Looking at them in relation to one another helps create a more connected design direction. Natural light, existing features and the mood you want from the space can all inform the palette. Rather than following a trend for its own sake, the aim is to explore combinations that reflect your preferences and work with the character of your interior.
                                </dd>
                            </div>
                            <div class="RelativePosition PaddingLeftSixteen">
                                <dt class="BaseTextSize SemiboldFont LeadingSeven TextGrayNineHundred">
                                    <div class="AbsolutePosition LeftZero TopZero FlexContainer HeightTen WidthTen ItemsCenterAlign JustifyContentCenter LargeRoundedCorners BackgroundSkySixHundred WhiteText">
                                        <svg class="WidthSix HeightSix" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" id="u0eci" data-name="Layer 1" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                                            <path
                                                d="m15.707,11.707l-2.293,2.293,2.293,2.293c.391.391.391,1.023,0,1.414-.195.195-.451.293-.707.293s-.512-.098-.707-.293l-2.293-2.293-2.293,2.293c-.195.195-.451.293-.707.293s-.512-.098-.707-.293c-.391-.391-.391-1.023,0-1.414l2.293-2.293-2.293-2.293c-.391-.391-.391-1.023,0-1.414s1.023-.391,1.414,0l2.293,2.293,2.293-2.293c.391-.391,1.023-.391,1.414,0s.391,1.023,0,1.414Zm7.293-6.707c0,.553-.448,1-1,1h-.885l-1.276,13.472c-.245,2.581-2.385,4.528-4.978,4.528h-5.727c-2.589,0-4.729-1.943-4.977-4.521l-1.296-13.479h-.86c-.552,0-1-.447-1-1s.448-1,1-1h4.101c.465-2.279,2.485-4,4.899-4h2c2.414,0,4.435,1.721,4.899,4h4.101c.552,0,1,.447,1,1Zm-14.828-1h7.656c-.413-1.164-1.524-2-2.828-2h-2c-1.304,0-2.415.836-2.828,2Zm10.934,2H4.87l1.278,13.287c.148,1.547,1.432,2.713,2.986,2.713h5.727c1.556,0,2.84-1.168,2.987-2.718l1.258-13.282Z"
                                            ></path>
                                        </svg>
                                    </div>
                                    Make Room for Practical Details
                                </dt>
                                <dd class="MarginTopTwo BaseTextSize LeadingSeven TextGraySixHundred">
                                    An interior should be considered as well as attractive. Access routes, furniture scale, storage and the way daylight changes through a room all influence how comfortable a layout may feel. Discussing these details early can help clarify priorities and highlight questions to resolve before making choices. Each space is different, so decisions should respond to its dimensions, intended use and the needs you share rather than rely on a one-size-fits-all formula.
                                </dd>
                            </div>
                            <div class="RelativePosition PaddingLeftSixteen">
                                <dt class="BaseTextSize SemiboldFont LeadingSeven TextGrayNineHundred">
                                    <div class="AbsolutePosition LeftZero TopZero FlexContainer HeightTen WidthTen ItemsCenterAlign JustifyContentCenter LargeRoundedCorners BackgroundSkySixHundred WhiteText">
                                        <svg class="WidthSix HeightSix" fill="currentColor" id="u0eci" height="512" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="512" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" data-name="Layer 1">
                                            <path d="m9 10a1 1 0 1 1 1 1 1 1 0 0 1 -1-1zm5 1a1 1 0 1 0 -1-1 1 1 0 0 0 1 1zm-4 2a1 1 0 1 0 1 1 1 1 0 0 0 -1-1zm4 2a1 1 0 1 0 -1-1 1 1 0 0 0 1 1zm10-5v4a5.006 5.006 0 0 1 -5 5h-14a5.006 5.006 0 0 1 -5-5v-4a5.006 5.006 0 0 1 5-5h14a5.006 5.006 0 0 1 5 5zm-17-3v10h10v-10zm-2 10v-10a3 3 0 0 0 -3 3v4a3 3 0 0 0 3 3zm17-7a3 3 0 0 0 -3-3v10a3 3 0 0 0 3-3z"></path>
                                        </svg>
                                    </div>
                                    Keep Your Preferences at the Centre
                                </dt>
                                <dd class="MarginTopTwo BaseTextSize LeadingSeven TextGraySixHundred">
                                    Design is personal, and a useful conversation makes space for your references, dislikes, routines and budget considerations without assuming a particular look. Sharing images or describing what you want a room to feel like can help establish a direction. Ideas can then be explored in context, with attention to how each choice relates to the rest of the space. The result of this approach is a design process guided by your brief, not by a fixed signature style.
                                </dd>
                            </div>
                        </dl>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
