                    <div class="MarginXAuto MaxWidthTwoXL LargeBreakpointMarginXZero LargeBreakpointMaxWidthNone">
                        <h2 class="TextSizeThreeXL BoldFont TightTracking TextGrayNineHundred SmallBreakpointTextSizeFourXL">A Clear Framework for Design Decisions</h2>
                        <div class="MarginTopSix FlexContainer FlexDirectionColumn GapXEight GapYTwenty LargeBreakpointFlexDirectionRow">
                            <div class="LargeBreakpointWidthFull LargeBreakpointMaxWidthTwoXL LargeBreakpointFlexGrowAuto">
                                <p class="TextSizeXL LeadingEight TextGraySixHundred">Every interior begins with different needs, dimensions and preferences, so the most useful first step is a thoughtful conversation. The framework below describes areas to consider when developing an interior design direction; it is not a record of completed projects or a promise of a particular result.</p>
                                <p class="MarginTopTen MaxWidthXL BaseTextSize LeadingSeven TextGraySevenHundred">
                                    Room planning involves connected decisions rather than a single stylistic choice. A brief can help bring the intended use of a space into focus, while layout, palette, materials and lighting provide practical and visual subjects to explore. These four headings are prompts for discussion, not performance statistics. The right priorities depend on your room, your preferences and the details you share.
                                </p>
                            </div>
                            <div class="LargeBreakpointFlex LargeBreakpointFlexGrowAuto LargeBreakpointJustifyCenter">
                                <dl class="WidthSixtyFour SpaceYEight ExtraLargeBreakpointWidthEighty">
                                    <div class="FlexContainer FlexDirectionColumnReverse GapYFour">
                                        <dt class="BaseTextSize LeadingSeven TextGraySixHundred">Understand the brief</dt>
                                        <dd class="TextSizeFiveXL SemiboldFont TightTracking TextGrayNineHundred">01</dd>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="FlexContainer FlexDirectionColumnReverse GapYFour">
                                        <dt class="BaseTextSize LeadingSeven TextGraySixHundred">Explore the layout</dt>
                                        <dd class="TextSizeFiveXL SemiboldFont TightTracking TextGrayNineHundred">02</dd>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="FlexContainer FlexDirectionColumnReverse GapYFour">
                                        <dt class="BaseTextSize LeadingSeven TextGraySixHundred">Consider colour and materials</dt>
                                        <dd class="TextSizeFiveXL SemiboldFont TightTracking TextGrayNineHundred">03</dd>
                                    </div>
                                </dl>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div id="qu16d">
            <div class="BackgroundWhite BorderYDirection">
                <div class="MarginXAuto MaxWidthSevenXL PaddingXSix PaddingYSixteen SmallBreakpointPaddingYTwentyFour LargeBreakpointPaddingXEight">
                    <div class="MarginXAuto MaxWidthTwoXL TextCenterAlignment">
                        <h2 class="TextSizeTwoXL BoldFont LeadingTen TightTracking TextGrayNineHundred">Questions About Interior Design</h2>
                        <p class="MarginTopSix BaseTextSize LeadingSeven TextGraySixHundred">If you are thinking about changing a room, it is normal to have questions before you begin. These answers offer general guidance on the kinds of details that can help start a design conversation. Every space is different, so share the circumstances and priorities that matter to you when you get in touch.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="MarginTopTwenty">
                        <dl class="SpaceYSixteen SmallBreakpointGrid SmallBreakpointGridColumnsTwo SmallBreakpointGapXSix SmallBreakpointGapYSixteen SmallBreakpointSpaceYZero LargeBreakpointGapXTen">
                            <div>
                                <dt class="BaseTextSize SemiboldFont LeadingSeven TextGrayNineHundred">What should I include in my first enquiry?</dt>
                                <dd class="MarginTopTwo BaseTextSize LeadingSeven TextGraySixHundred">Briefly describe the space, what you would like to change and how you use it. You can also mention your preferences, questions and any practical considerations you would like to discuss.</dd>
                            </div>
                            <div>
                                <dt class="BaseTextSize SemiboldFont LeadingSeven TextGrayNineHundred">Can I ask about a single room?</dt>
                                <dd class="MarginTopTwo BaseTextSize LeadingSeven TextGraySixHundred">Yes. You can make an enquiry about one room or describe several connected spaces. The scope and next steps can be discussed based on the details of your project.</dd>
                            </div>
                            <div>
                                <dt class="BaseTextSize SemiboldFont LeadingSeven TextGrayNineHundred">Do I need to know my preferred style already?</dt>
                                <dd class="MarginTopTwo BaseTextSize LeadingSeven TextGraySixHundred">No. You can share colours, images or rooms you like, but it is also fine to begin with how you want the space to feel and function. Those preferences can help shape the conversation.</dd>
                            </div>
                            <div>
                                <dt class="BaseTextSize SemiboldFont LeadingSeven TextGrayNineHundred">Can existing furniture be part of the design discussion?</dt>
                                <dd class="MarginTopTwo BaseTextSize LeadingSeven TextGraySixHundred">Yes. Mention which pieces you would like to keep, along with any relevant measurements or photographs. This can help consider how existing furniture relates to the room and other design choices.</dd>
                            </div>
                        </dl>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
